1
00:00:01,247 --> 00:00:09,057
Meet Margin Post: a local-first workspace for reviewing Markdown changed by coding agents, scripts, and other external tools.

2
00:00:09,338 --> 00:00:12,268
It works without an account, and without a cloud dependency.

3
00:00:16,248 --> 00:00:19,562
Margin Post does not claim to block writes before they happen.

4
00:00:19,710 --> 00:00:21,970
External tools write to disk first.

5
00:00:22,413 --> 00:00:26,855
Margin Post captures the real filesystem result as a durable Change Set.

6
00:00:27,099 --> 00:00:30,039
Before any decision is applied, it checks the file again.

7
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:40,369
Open a local folder, and keep editing in a calm Markdown workspace.

8
00:00:40,779 --> 00:00:48,224
Agent, script, and manual changes enter a persistent review inbox, without interrupting your work or requiring you to understand Git.

9
00:00:56,249 --> 00:01:03,531
Review additions, deletions, and rewrites in document structure: including headings, paragraphs, lists, quotes, code, and tables.

10
00:01:04,025 --> 00:01:11,652
Accept or reject each change; use keyboard shortcuts; undo the last decision; and stop safely if the file changes again during review.

11
00:01:21,256 --> 00:01:23,469
File operations are explicit too.

12
00:01:23,637 --> 00:01:25,528
Rejecting a new file removes it.

13
00:01:25,850 --> 00:01:28,847
Rejecting a deletion restores its reviewed content.

14
00:01:29,150 --> 00:01:31,868
Rejecting a rename returns the previous path.

15
00:01:32,076 --> 00:01:36,443
Older candidates remain visible as superseded, instead of silently disappearing.

16
00:01:41,257 --> 00:01:44,418
Every accepted result enters local version history.

17
00:01:44,687 --> 00:01:48,514
Compare adjacent versions with the same structured Markdown engine.

18
00:01:48,925 --> 00:01:53,673
When restoring an earlier version, the current disk state is preserved as a recovery point.

19
00:01:55,126 --> 00:01:59,196
Margin Post keeps agent-edited Markdown reviewable, and recoverable.
